.TH voidpop "1" "March 2024" "voidpop version 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
voidpop \- dummy pop3 server
.SH SYNOPSIS
voidpop [\-c config] [\-d 1]
.SH DESCRIPTION
This program starts a dummy pop3 server that accepts any login and
reports no messages.
.SS Options
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
help
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
version information
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-config\fR <FILE>
use <CONFIG> for configuration (default: \fI\,/etc/fail2ban\-honeyd.conf\/\fP)
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-debug\fR [1|0]
turn debug on (default: off)
.SH FILES
.TP
\fC/etc/fail2ban\-honeyd.conf\fR
.SH "SEE ALSO"
fail2ban(1)
